The complete circuit-independent category/action/factor fixtures in
../prepared_noise_batches.rs are adapted from itpyi/magna revision
56847478c840395735146ef1e1ccdc3d8aedc10f:

- tests/core/test_file_reuse.py: FileReuseTests.test_prepared_noise_weights_and_batch_partition
- tests/core/test_packed_noise.py: PackedNoiseTests.test_sparse_actions_weights_and_partitioning
- tests/core/test_packed_noise.py: PackedNoiseTests.test_large_weight_group_without_count_table
- tests/core/test_weight_fast_paths.py: WeightFastPathTests.test_count_weights_match_independent_products_across_group_sizes
- tests/core/test_weight_fast_paths.py: WeightFastPathTests.test_grouped_factors_preserve_choices_and_unreduced_weights

The joint-law driver check also retains the independent six-sigma contract from
tests/core/test_packed_noise.py: test_marginals_and_joint_law_across_lanes_and_blocks.
The full MPL-2.0 license is in original_many_record_input.LICENSE beside this file.

Rust's SplitMix64, owned typed actions, exact arbitrary-rational physical law,
explicit resource admission, signed raw-factor constructor and forced rational
cutoff-boundary assertions are independent adaptations. No Python/Native seeded
stream, private object/allocator layout, or finite64 probability approximation
is claimed. Raw products retain numerator/denominator without reduction, while
input factors equal to one (including 3/3) are skipped as in the reference.
